---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: benchmarks
navKey: benchmarks
crumbKey: crumb.benchmarks
title: "Benchmarks — Citere"
description: "Every Citere measurement in one place: repeat-rate and source contamination per assistant, question type, country and narrative cluster. Never averaged."
schemas:
  - dataset
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/benchmarks/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- set doc = copy.en.benchmarks -%}
<div class="phead"><h1>{{ doc.data.h1 }}</h1>
  <p class="plead">{{ doc.data.lead | mdInline | safe }}</p></div>

<div class="callout"><b>This page is a shell.</b> A benchmark is one cluster over one month, and the full
  issue is not specified yet. What is published below is the figure set that is settled: the coverage of
  each issue, the grain-of-truth split, and the A&times;B matrix. Everything per-assistant and per-market
  lives on the pages that own it &mdash; each assistant, each market, and each claim &mdash; and is
  reached from the issue below.</div>

<h2 id="issues" style="margin:30px 0 6px">Issues</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">One issue per cluster per month. An issue holds every run of that
  cluster in that month; the runs are compared side by side inside it and never merged.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Benchmark issues, newest first</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Issue</th><th scope="col">Cluster</th><th scope="col" class="num">Markets</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Claims</th><th scope="col" class="num">Answers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for issue in benchmarks.issues %}
    <tr><th scope="row" style="font-weight:400"><a href="{{ issue.url | url }}">{{ issue.monthLabel }}</a></th>
      <td style="color:var(--dim)">{{ issue.clusterName }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.markets | length }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.claimsCount }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ issue.responses }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="grain" style="margin:30px 0 6px">The grain-of-truth split</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Claims built on a real event against claims invented outright, by
  question type, in {{ benchmarks.marketName }} in {{ benchmarks.label }}. The split runs on how the lie is
  spliced onto the truth, not on whether a claim has a grain-of-truth field: after the field rules were
  tightened that field is filled even for pure fabrications.</p>
<div class="panel"><table>
  <caption class="visually-hidden">Repeat rate on claims built on a real event against pure fabrications, by question type</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">{{ 'col.persona' | t }}</th><th scope="col" class="num">Real event underneath</th>
    <th scope="col" class="num">Invented outright</th><th scope="col">Difference</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for row in benchmarks.grain_of_truth %}
    <tr data-persona="{{ row.persona }}">
      <th scope="row" class="mono" style="font-weight:400;font-size:12px;color:var(--dimmer)">{{ row.persona }} &middot; {{ row.persona | personaLabel }}</th>
      <td class="num">{{ row.with_grain | rate }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.pure | rate }}</td>
      <td style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12.5px">{{ "significant" if row.significant else "not significant" }}</td></tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="abx" style="margin:30px 0 6px">A&times;B matrix</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Every answer in {{ benchmarks.marketName }}, {{ benchmarks.label }},
  placed by what the assistant did and whether it cited a listed source.</p>
{% include "partials/abx-matrix.njk" %}

<h2 id="funnel" style="margin:30px 0 6px">From answers to incidents</h2>
<p class="note" style="margin:0 0 14px">Across every run held here. The A&times;B intersection is the filter:
  it is what turns raw source flags into the few cases worth a person's time.</p>
{% include "partials/funnel.njk" %}

<div class="exports" style="margin:26px 0 44px">
  {%- if benchmarks.issues | length %}<a href="{{ '/registry/reports.csv' | url }}">Every metric cell as CSV</a><span>&middot;</span>{% endif %}
  <a href="{{ '/countries/full/' | url }}">The full market breakdown</a><span>&middot;</span>
  <a href="{{ '/data/' | url }}">All exports</a></div>
